 R←Test_Dir2_038(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;list;list2
⍝ Test the `Dir2` method recursively with depths←1. Should only return the given folder and its sub-folders and the content.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 list←⊃('recurse' 1)##.FilesAndDirs.Dir2 ∆Home,'/'

 list2←⊃('recurse' 1)('depth' 1)##.FilesAndDirs.Dir2 ∆Home,'/'
 →T.PassesIf(≢list2)<≢list
 →T.PassesIf 0 1≡∪{+/⍵∊'/\'}¨(1+≢∆Home)↓¨list2

 list2←⊃('recurse' 1)('depth' 2)##.FilesAndDirs.Dir2 ∆Home,'/'
 →T.PassesIf(≢list2)<≢list
 →T.PassesIf 0 1 2≡∪{+/⍵∊'/\'}¨(1+≢∆Home)↓¨list2

 R←T._OK
